<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="58.1" level="1">Taxation</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="I" level="2">Taxes Administered by the Department of Taxation</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="3" level="3">Income Tax</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="6" level="4">Taxation of Estates and Trusts</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>58.1-360</section_number>
	<catch_line>Imposition of tax</catch_line>
	<text>
		A tax is hereby annually imposed, at the rates prescribed by § 58.1-320 for individuals, on the Virginia taxable income for each taxable year of every estate and trust.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, §§ 58-151.03, 58-151.021; 1971 Ex. Sess., c. 171; 1972, c. 310; 1978, cc. 159, 796; 1981, c. 402; 1984, c. 675.</history>
</law>
